 "title": "Square and cube numbers",
 "audience": "learner",
 "keyIdea": "A square number is n × n (written n²); a cube number is n × n × n (written n³).",
 "explain": {
  "kid": [
   "Make a square with 3 rows of 3 tiles. That is 9 tiles. So 9 is a square number. We write 3² = 9.",
   "Stack 3 layers of 3 by 3 cubes. That is 27 cubes, so 27 is a cube number: 3³ = 27."
  ],
  "adult": [
   "n² (n squared) means n × n; the name comes from the square of tiles. n³ (n cubed) means n × n × n; the name comes from a cube of blocks.",
   "The first square numbers are 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36, 49, 64, 81, 100. The first cubes are 1, 8, 27, 64, 125. 64 is both: 8² and 4³. A common mistake is 3² = 6: squaring is not doubling."
  ]
 },
